Training robot foundation models faces two key hurdles: obtaining enough data to train an effective model and ensuring that new skills can be acquired quickly. The team at @RhodaAI believes that training Direct Video Action models from web data is the solution. Web data is plentiful, allowing Rhoda to train their base model on hundreds of years of video data. With the addition of robot data, they can quickly adapt it to new tasks with as little as 20 hours of in-domain data, performing complex, multi-step manipulation tasks with their purpose-built video foundation model.

@RoboPapers: "Watch Episode #79 of RoboPapers, with @micoolcho, @chris_j_paxton, and @DJiafei, to learn more!"

