Robotics involves understanding how things change in response to actions and forces, which cannot be learned from static images. Instead, learning from video is more effective and data-efficient.

@elvisnavah discusses @mimicrobotic, highlighting that pretraining on web-scale video allows robots to acquire physics priors. This leads to policies that train faster, generalize better, and achieve more impressive dexterity compared to training on static images or image-language pairs as in a vision-language model.

