The linked paper introduces VE2VF, a method for distilling vision-enabled policies into vision-free ones, enabling robots to perform contact-rich manipulation tasks without relying on visual input.

Played their prototype a few weeks ago—very impressive. It is low backlash, highly backdrivable, and has relatively low gear ratios. This gave a sense that an inflection point is approaching, similar to the feeling when first touching the Unitree G1 in 2024. Many teams like Sharpa, WuJi, and RobotEra are building in this space, and 2026 is expected to be a breakthrough year for dexterous hands.

